---
description: MCP tool action classification and approval policy
alwaysApply: true
---

The canonical MCP policy lives in `docs/MCP_WORKFLOW.md`, MCP Tool Policy. Classify every MCP action — and every external-tool write through a CLI such as `gh` — before calling it:

- **READ** — may run without approval (inspect a local/approved staging schema,
  search files, read PRs).
- **REVERSIBLE WRITE** — state the target and intended change before executing (create a branch, update a draft, modify a local or approved staging development record).
- **HIGH IMPACT** — explicit user approval required (application or service
  deploy, non-account deletion outside a production database, credential
  changes outside a production database, force push, destructive
  local/approved staging migration, mass update on local/approved staging).
- **FORBIDDEN** — never perform, even with chat approval (account deletion on
  any environment — local, staging, or production; production database reads,
  including schema inspection, writes, drops, deletes, migrations, or
  credentials).

Standing principles: read before write; use the narrowest tool available, never
a broader one when a narrower exists; never silently switch from a development
target to a production target; never treat production DB work or agent-executed
account deletion as approvable; never expose credential values
(`docs/SECURITY.md`). Agents may implement and non-destructively validate the
protected account-deletion flow and prepare a checklist, but an actual deletion
must be initiated and executed manually by a human, never through an
agent-controlled browser, MCP, SQL, or admin tool.

GitHub Project #4 via `gh`: listing is READ; the writes on the PR body's
`Project #4 moves:` line (card moves, item creation with all fields, detail
edits, archive, README pointer) are REVERSIBLE WRITEs that the agent applies
after human approval, one approved write per listed item however many `gh`
calls it takes — the human reviews and approves, the agent executes; bulk or
unlisted writes, schema changes, or `Completed` without ledger
acceptance are HIGH IMPACT; item or project deletion is FORBIDDEN. The board
mirrors `docs/TASKS.md` and never leads it (`docs/DOCUMENTATION_POLICY.md`,
GitHub Project #4 Mirror).
